भूतभावन भूतेश देवदेव जगत्पते ॥ १५ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2934,\"bb\":2598,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2598/\",\"body_value\":\"svayam evātmanātmānaṁ
vettha tvaṁ puruṣottama
bhūta-bhāvana bhūteśa
deva-deva jagat-pate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2935,\"bb\":2599,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2599/\",\"shadow_value\":\"svayam – personally; eva – certainly; ātmanā – by Yourself; ātmānam – Yourself; vettha – know; tvam – You; puruṣa-uttama – O greatest of all persons; bhūta-bhāvana – O origin of everything; bhūta-īśa – O Lord of everything; deva-deva – O Lord of all demigods; jagat-pate – O Lord of the entire universe.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"svayam\",\"translation\":\"personally\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"ātmanā\",\"translation\":\"by Yourself\"},{\"word\":\"ātmānam\",\"translation\":\"Yourself\"},{\"word\":\"vettha\",\"translation\":\"know\"},{\"word\":\"tvam\",\"translation\":\"You\"},{\"word\":\"puruṣa-uttama\",\"translation\":\"O greatest of all persons\"},{\"word\":\"bhūta-bhāvana\",\"translation\":\"O origin of everything\"},{\"word\":\"bhūta-īśa\",\"translation\":\"O Lord of everything\"},{\"word\":\"deva-deva\",\"translation\":\"O Lord of all demigods\"},{\"word\":\"jagat-pate\",\"translation\":\"O Lord of the entire universe\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2936,\"bb\":2600,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2600/\",\"body_value\":\"Indeed, You alone know Yourself by Your own internal potency, O Supreme Person, origin of all, Lord of all beings, God of gods, Lord of the universe!\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2937,\"bb\":2601,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2601/\",\"body_value\":\"The Supreme Lord, Kṛṣṇa, can be known by persons who are in a relationship with Him through the discharge of devotional service, like Arjuna and his followers. Persons of demonic or atheistic mentality cannot know Kṛṣṇa. Mental speculation that leads one away from the Supreme Lord is a serious sin, and one who does not know Kṛṣṇa should not try to comment on Bhagavad-gītā. Bhagavad-gītā is the statement of Kṛṣṇa, and since it is the science of Kṛṣṇa, it should be understood from Kṛṣṇa as Arjuna understood it. It should not be received from atheistic persons.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2938,\"bb\":2602,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2602/\",\"body_value\":\" As stated in Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam (1.2.11):\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2939,\"bb\":2603,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2603/\",\"body_value\":\"vadanti tat tattva-vidas
tattvaṁ yaj jñānam advayam
brahmeti paramātmeti
bhagavān iti śabdyate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2940,\"bb\":2604,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/15/b2604/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 10.15\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 10.15\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/10/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/10/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"chil